diff --git a/service/fluxyinspector/README.md b/service/fluxyinspector/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b6ce06b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/service/fluxyinspector/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Fluxy inspector service
+
+This service embeds the HTTP/HTTPS, HTTP/2/gRPC and WebSocket inspection engine
+from Fluxy's retired standalone goproxy module. The implementation is included in this source
+tree; it does not require a local checkout of Fluxy to compile. The engine's
+original code is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). Its dependencies keep their own
+licenses and versions in the top-level go.mod/go.sum.
+
+## Inspector process configuration
+
+Fluxy runs one sing-box process: Electron owns it in proxy mode, and the Helper
+owns it in TUN mode. This example is for **proxy mode**, generated by Fluxy's
+`src/main/capture/sing-box-proxy.ts`. It matches the generated configuration with
+loopback listening enabled and port 6060. The listen address and port follow the
+application settings.
+
+
+```json
+{
+  "log": {"level": "info", "output": "stderr", "disabled": false, "timestamp": false},
+  "services": [{"type": "fluxy-inspector", "tag": "inspector"}],
+  "inbounds": [{"type": "fluxy-mixed", "tag": "proxy", "listen": "127.0.0.1", "listen_port": 6060}],
+  "outbounds": [{"type": "fluxy-inspect", "tag": "inspect", "inspector": "inspector"}],
+  "route": {"final": "inspect", "rules": [{"network": "udp", "action": "reject"}]}
+}
+```
+
+### Which generated file to inspect
+
+On macOS, the default application data directory is
+`~/Library/Application Support/dev.fengqi.fluxy.electron` (`FLUXY_DATA_DIR` can
+override it).
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `<data>/proxy-core-*/config.json` | Proxy mode; contains `services: fluxy-inspector`, a `fluxy-mixed` inbound and a `fluxy-inspect` outbound. |
+| `/Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/dev.fengqi.fluxy.electron.helper/json` | Combined TUN and inspector configuration actually passed to the single privileged process, generated by `helper/internal/tun/params.go`. The filename has no `.json` extension. |
+
+The TUN configuration includes the same `fluxy-inspector` service and in-process
+`fluxy-inspect` outbound. It adds the `tun` capture inbound, an authenticated HTTP
+egress inbound, and direct-egress routing; scoped capture adds DNS/FakeIP rules.
+It also keeps the public `fluxy-mixed` inbound. Electron connects to the Helper's
+one-use loopback control relay with the session token, and the Helper forwards
+IPC to the core's inherited stdin/stdout. There is no second sing-box process or
+HTTP inspection bridge. The `tun.ready` RPC completes network/DNS setup after
+the inspector receives its start frame.
+
+Addresses, ports, credentials, routes and domain rules are generated from the
+current session and settings. Runtime files are cleaned up on stop; change their
+generators for persistent configuration changes.
+
+The root CA identity and inspection policies are delivered over IPC rather than
+stored in the sing-box configuration JSON.
+
+### Controller startup
+
+Start with `sing-box run -c config.json`. The controller must send the existing
+Fluxy length-prefixed JSON `start` message over stdin, including the root CA
+identity and `ingressPort`. stdout is exclusively framed IPC, and logs go to
+stderr. The response is `{"type":"ready","port":6060,"in_process":true}`.
+The port describes the public ingress; no private inspection port is opened.
+
+Request/response policies, custom server certificates, breakpoints, streaming
+credits and cancellation continue to use Fluxy's existing IPC messages. A full
+Fluxy controller is required; this is not an autonomous MITM service.
+
+`fluxy-inspect` resolves the inspector service by tag and uses in-memory streams.
+Original client identity is carried separately from HTTP headers. TCP streams
+from SOCKS/TUN enter the same CONNECT policy and TLS interception path. Existing
+`server_port`/`token` outbound settings still use the separate-process inspection
+endpoint; they cannot be combined with `inspector`.
+
+Only one inspector can own stdin/stdout. The service closes its connections and
+requests sing-box shutdown on control EOF or failure. SIGTERM closes the service
+normally. Helper stdin monitoring does not read concurrently with IPC. SIGHUP
+reload is declined for inspector instances; restart the controller-owned process.
+Configuration via `-c stdin` and logging to stdout are incompatible with IPC.
+
+Go embedders must attach exclusive `io.ReadCloser`/`io.WriteCloser` control streams
+using `WithControl(ctx, input, output, shutdown)` before constructing the Box.
+The shutdown callback must cancel the owning instance. Closing the inspector also
+closes its control streams. Proxy mode uses the desktop process. TUN mode runs
+the inspector inside the Helper-owned core, including its elevated privileges.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+go test -race -mod=readonly -tags=with_gvisor,with_fluxy -ldflags=-checklinkname=0 ./service/fluxyinspector/... ./include ./cmd/sing-box
+```
